critical-mass-5ca59b8a.conceptual_definition:
The formula for the Jeans Mass (
$M_J$
) quantifies the minimum mass a cloud of gas must possess to overcome internal thermal pressure and collapse under its own gravity, leading to star formation. It represents a critical threshold where gravitational instability dominates over thermal support.

