kinetic-energy-curvilinear.conceptual_definition:
The formula describes the kinetic energy (
            \(T\)
            ) of a point mass or a system of particles in a general curvilinear coordinate system. It generalizes the familiar Cartesian form (
            \(T = \frac{1}{2} m v^2\)
            ) by incorporating the metric tensor to account for the geometry of the coordinate system and the velocities expressed in these generalized coordinates.
